  "adjudication": [
    "A first centered water-storage moment over the 0-140 cm long layer does not provide a broadly supported replacement for explicit local resolution.",
    "Both moment reconstructions lower the worst flux error but increase pooled RMS and mean-absolute error, and both worsen all three S2 primary cases on RMS and maximum error.",
    "The same four-scalar budget used as four explicit storages (L4) is substantially more faithful than L3 plus one global first moment in this B01 fixed-flux operator test.",
    "The evidence therefore favors local placement of the fourth scalar near the active long-to-local interface, not additional global long-layer memory.",
    "Because W_0_140 plus W_130_140 is algebraically equivalent to the L4 split W_0_130 plus W_130_140, there is no distinct four-state 'L3 plus local-band' family to test."
  ],
  "next": "Adopt L4 as the first explicit-resolution four-state control/candidate for cross-boundary-regime evaluation; do not add a second global moment before testing the prescribed-head frontier.",
